THE DECISIONS — facts, not claims to re-litigate:
- A session cannot change its own effort for good; a skill's frontmatter `effort` applies to the rest of the turn it is invoked in and is cleared at the next user prompt (documented in Claude Code's skills page; measured in live-probe.txt).
- One session (the lead keeps the conversation), not a handover at his yes.
- The flag is per session id in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dxb-design-max/; the close command takes the id from CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, which equals the hook's stdin session_id (measured).
- Opening the mode is the lead's judgment on the first design turn (the door and the skill's description tell it); the hook only holds it open across turns.
- The project hook runs in every session opened in this repository; the company's own Claude calls run with their own Claude home and settingSources [] (runtime isolation, 2026-10-03) and do not load it.

